+## 24. INDIAN PARLIAMENTARY GROUP
+
+**[SYL: GS2-C.2] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 24]**
+
+### 24.1. Introduction
+
+The **Indian Parliamentary Group (IPG)** is an autonomous body formed in 1949 to promote personal contacts between members of Parliament and to study questions of public importance. It functions as the **National Group** of the Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) and the main link between Indian Parliament and various parliaments of the world.
+
+### 24.2. Composition
+
+- All members of Parliament (Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha) are ex-officio members of the Group.
+- The Speaker of Lok Sabha is the ex-officio President of the Group.
+- The Deputy Speaker of Lok Sabha and Deputy Chairman of Rajya Sabha are ex-officio Vice-Presidents.
+- The Secretary-General of Lok Sabha functions as the Secretary of the Group.
+
+### 24.3. Objectives
+
+- To promote closer relations with other parliaments and parliamentary institutions.
+- To exchange information on parliamentary procedure, practice and institutions.
+- To discuss matters of common interest and promote peaceful cooperation among nations.
+- To represent India at IPU conferences, Commonwealth Parliamentary Association (CPA) meetings and other international forums.
+
+### 24.4. Functions
+
+- Arranges visits of foreign parliamentary delegations to India and deputes Indian parliamentary delegations abroad.
+- Provides information to MPs on international parliamentary developments.
+- Organises seminars, discussions and lectures on parliamentary and international issues.
+- Acts as India's link with IPU and CPA.
+
+### 24.5. Significance
+
+- Promotes parliamentary diplomacy.
+- Enhances India's image and strengthens bilateral/parliamentary ties.
+- Provides platform for exchange of democratic experiences.
+
+### 24.6. PYQs
+
+| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 2016 | Prelims | Indian Parliamentary Group is affiliated to? | IPG | Inter-Parliamentary Union (IPU) |
+| 2017 | Prelims | Speaker of Lok Sabha is ex-officio _____ of IPG? | IPG | President |
+
+### 24.7. MIND MAP
+
+```text
+INDIAN PARLIAMENTARY GROUP
+├── ESTABLISHED: 1949 (Autonomous body)
+├── AFFILIATION: National Group of IPU, link with CPA
+├── PRESIDENT: Speaker of Lok Sabha (ex-officio)
+├── MEMBERS: All MPs (ex-officio)
+└── FUNCTIONS: Delegations, IPU/CPA representation, parliamentary diplomacy
+```
