## 26. GOVERNOR

**[SYL: GS2-D.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 26] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 153-162]**

### 26.1. Introduction

Governor is the **constitutional head** of the state, analogous to President at the Union level. Article 153 provides for Governor for each state. Same person can be appointed as Governor for two or more states (Art. 153 proviso).

### 26.2. APPOINTMENT OF GOVERNOR (ART. 155)

Appointed by the **President** by warrant under his hand and seal. Governor holds office during the pleasure of the President (Art. 156). Usually holds office for a term of **5 years**, but can be removed earlier.

### 26.3. QUALIFICATIONS (ART. 157-158)

- **Art. 157:** Must be a citizen of India and have completed age of **35 years**.
- **Art. 158:** Must not hold any office of profit, must not be a member of Parliament/State Legislature.

### 26.4. OATH OR AFFIRMATION (ART. 159)

Administered by the **Chief Justice of the High Court** of the concerned state, or in his absence, the senior-most judge of that High Court.

### 26.5. POWERS AND FUNCTIONS OF GOVERNOR

#### 26.5.1. Executive Powers
- Appoints Chief Minister and other ministers on CM's advice.
- Appoints Advocate General, Chairman and members of State Public Service Commission (on President's approval for removal).
- Appoints judges of District Courts in consultation with High Court.
- Can seek information from CM regarding administration and legislative proposals.
- Recommends President's Rule in state (Art. 356).

#### 26.5.2. Legislative Powers (Arts. 168-213)
- Summons, prorogues and dissolves the State Legislature.
- Addresses State Legislature at commencement of first session after each general election and first session of each year (Art. 176).
- Can send messages to House(s) with respect to pending bills (Art. 175(2)).
- Nominates 1/6 members of Legislative Council from persons with special knowledge/experience in literature, science, art, cooperative movement, social service (Art. 171).
- Nominates Anglo-Indian members to Legislative Assembly if not adequately represented (Art. 333).
- Gives assent, withholds assent or reserves bills for President's consideration (Art. 200).
- Can promulgate ordinances when Legislature is not in session (Art. 213).

#### 26.5.3. Financial Powers
- Causes Annual Financial Statement (Budget) to be laid before Legislature (Art. 202).
- Money Bills can be introduced only with Governor's recommendation (Art. 207).
- Can make advances out of Contingency Fund of State (Art. 205).
- Recommends grant for certain purposes.

#### 26.5.4. Judicial Powers
- Pardons, reprieves, respites or remissions of punishment or suspends, remits or commutes sentences in certain cases (Art. 161).
- Consults High Court on appointment of District Judges.
- Makes appointments to judicial services below District Judge level in consultation with State PSC and High Court.

#### 26.5.5. Discretionary Powers
Governor acts on aid and advice of Council of Ministers **except** in situations where Constitution requires him to act in discretion:
- Appointment of CM in case of no clear majority / hung assembly
- Dismissal of a ministry that has lost confidence but refuses to resign
- Dissolution of Assembly if CM advises dissolution but Council of Ministers has lost majority
- Recommendation of President's Rule (Art. 356)
- Reservation of a bill for President's consideration
- Seeking information from CM
- Any other matter where Constitution expressly allows discretion

### 26.6. Governor's Role - Important Points

- **Constitutional head, not executive head:** Real executive is Council of Ministers headed by CM.
- **Agent of Centre:** Often criticised for acting as Centre's representative.
- **Dual role:** Constitutional head of state + representative of Centre.
- **Position analogous to President:** Same constitutional principles apply.

### 26.7. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Governor holds office during pleasure of? | Appointment | President |
| 2017 | Mains | Discretionary powers of Governor - scope and misuse | Discretionary Powers | Sarkaria Commission recommendations |
| 2018 | Prelims | Ordinance making power of Governor is under which Article? | Ordinance | Article 213 |
| 2019 | Mains | Role of Governor in a hung Assembly | Discretion | Constitutional conventions + discretion |

### 26.8. MIND MAP

```text
GOVERNOR (ARTS. 153-162)
├── APPOINTMENT: By President, holds office during President's pleasure (5 years)
├── POWERS
│   ├── Executive: Appoints CM/Ministers, recommends President's Rule
│   ├── Legislative: Summon/prorogue/dissolve, assent/reserve bills, ordinances (Art. 213)
│   ├── Financial: Budget, Money Bill recommendation
│   └── Judicial: Pardoning power (Art. 161)
├── DISCRETIONARY: Hung Assembly, President's Rule, bill reservation etc.
└── CONSTITUTIONAL HEAD (acts on aid & advice) except discretionary cases
```

