## 27. CHIEF MINISTER

**[SYL: GS2-D.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 27] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 163-164]**

### 27.1. Introduction

Chief Minister is the **real executive authority** in the state. Article 163 provides for Council of Ministers headed by CM to aid and advise Governor. Article 164 deals with other provisions as to Ministers.

### 27.2. APPOINTMENT OF CHIEF MINISTER

Appointed by the **Governor**. In case of single party majority, leader of majority party is appointed. In case of hung assembly, Governor uses discretion to appoint CM (usually leader of largest party/coalition who can form stable government).

### 27.3. POWERS AND FUNCTIONS OF CHIEF MINISTER

#### 27.3.1. In Relation to Council of Ministers
- **Formation:** Recommends names of persons to be appointed as ministers to Governor.
- **Allocation of portfolios:** Allocates and reshuffles portfolios among ministers.
- **Chairman of Cabinet:** Presides over Cabinet meetings.
- **Coordination:** Ensures coordination among different departments.
- **Dismissal:** Can ask a minister to resign or advise Governor to dismiss him in case of difference of opinion.

#### 27.3.2. In Relation to Governor
- Acts as principal channel of communication between Governor and Council of Ministers (Art. 167).
- Advises Governor on appointment of important officials (Advocate General, Chairman of State PSC etc.).
- Recommends summoning, prorogation and dissolution of Legislature.
- Furnishes information to Governor as required.

#### 27.3.3. In Relation to State Legislature
- Announces government policies on floor of House.
- Advises Governor with respect to legislation.
- Seeks vote of confidence/support.
- Pilots important bills.

#### 27.3.4. Other Functions
- Leader of the House in Legislative Assembly (usually).
- Crisis management and advisor to Governor in discretionary situations.
- Represents state in inter-state councils and NITI Aayog meetings.

### 27.4. Chief Minister and Council of Ministers - Relationship

- Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to Legislative Assembly (Art. 164).
- CM is the link between Governor and Council of Ministers.
- If CM loses confidence of Assembly, entire Council of Ministers must resign.
- Ministers hold office during pleasure of Governor but cannot continue without CM's support.

### 27.5. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to? | Responsibility | Legislative Assembly (Art. 164) |
| 2017 | Mains | Role of Chief Minister in state administration | CM's Role | Link between Governor & Ministers, leadership of Council |
| 2018 | Prelims | Who advises Governor on summoning/dissolving State Legislature? | Powers | Chief Minister on behalf of Council of Ministers |

### 27.6. MIND MAP

```text
CHIEF MINISTER
├── APPOINTMENT: By Governor (leader of majority party)
├── RELATION WITH COUNCIL: Head, allocates portfolios, coordinates
├── RELATION WITH GOVERNOR: Principal channel, advises on key matters
├── RELATION WITH LEGISLATURE: Leader of House, accountable
└── COLLECTIVE RESPONSIBILITY: To Legislative Assembly (Art. 164)
```

