## 28. STATE COUNCIL OF MINISTERS

**[SYL: GS2-D.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 28] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 163-164, 166-167]**

### 28.1. Constitution of Council of Ministers

Article 163(1): There shall be a Council of Ministers with the Chief Minister at the head to aid and advise the Governor in the exercise of his functions, except in so far as he is by or under this Constitution required to exercise his functions or any of them in his discretion.

Article 164(1): The Chief Minister shall be appointed by the Governor and the other Ministers shall be appointed by the Governor on the advice of the Chief Minister.

### 28.2. Categories of Ministers

- **Cabinet Ministers:** Head important ministries, members of Cabinet (inner ring). Formulate policy.
- **Ministers of State:** Can be independent charge of departments or attached to Cabinet Ministers.
- **Deputy Ministers:** Assist Cabinet/State Ministers, not members of Cabinet, rarely used now.

### 28.3. Principles of Ministerial Responsibility

- **Individual Responsibility (Art. 164):** Ministers hold office during pleasure of Governor but are individually responsible to Legislature for their department.
- **Collective Responsibility (Art. 164):** Council of Ministers is collectively responsible to the Legislative Assembly of the state. If no-confidence motion passed, entire Council resigns.
- **Secrecy:** Ministers take oath of secrecy (Art. 164(3)).

### 28.4. Functions

- Formulates and implements state policies.
- Prepares budget and legislation.
- Advises Governor on exercise of executive powers.
- Ensures law and order, development and welfare measures.

### 28.5. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Ministers hold office during pleasure of? | Responsibility | Governor (Art. 164) |
| 2019 | Prelims | Collective responsibility means? | Responsibility | To Legislative Assembly |

### 28.6. MIND MAP

```text
STATE COUNCIL OF MINISTERS (ARTS. 163-164)
├── COMPOSITION: CM + Ministers (Cabinet, MoS, Deputy)
├── COLLECTIVE RESPONSIBILITY: To Legislative Assembly
├── INDIVIDUAL RESPONSIBILITY: To Legislature for own department
└── OATH OF SECRECY & OFFICE
```

