## 29. STATE LEGISLATURE

**[SYL: GS2-D.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 29] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 168-212]**

### 29.1. Organisation of State Legislature (Art. 168)

State Legislature consists of:
- **Governor** + **Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)** - in states with unicameral legislature
- **Governor** + **Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)** + **Legislative Assembly** - in states with bicameral legislature

Currently 6 states have Legislative Councils (Andhra Pradesh, Bihar, Karnataka, Maharashtra, Telangana, Uttar Pradesh).

### 29.2. Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha)

- **Composition:** Not more than 500, not less than 60 members (Art. 170). Directly elected by people on basis of adult franchise.
- **Term:** 5 years unless dissolved earlier.
- **Speaker & Deputy Speaker:** Elected by members.
- **Money Bills:** Can only be introduced in Legislative Assembly. Council has limited powers.

### 29.3. Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad)

- **Composition:** Not more than 1/3 of Assembly strength, not less than 40 members (Art. 171).
- **Members elected/nominated by various constituencies:** MLAs, local bodies, graduates, teachers, Governor's nominees.
- **Term:** 6 years, 1/3 retire every 2 years (permanent house like Rajya Sabha).
- **Chairman & Deputy Chairman:** Elected by members.

### 29.4. Powers and Functions

- **Legislative:** Can make laws on subjects in State List and Concurrent List.
- **Financial:** Control over finances, budget passed by Assembly.
- **Executive control:** Questions, motions, no-confidence motion (only in Assembly).
- **Constituent:** Ratifies constitutional amendments under Art. 368 requiring state ratification.

### 29.5. Differences between Assembly and Council

| Feature | Legislative Assembly | Legislative Council |
|---|---|---|
| **Nature** | Popular House, directly elected | Indirectly elected + nominated |
| **Powers** | More powerful (Money Bills, confidence motion) | Less powerful |
| **Term** | 5 years (dissolvable) | 6 years (permanent, 1/3 retire) |
| **Money Bills** | Originates here, Council cannot reject | Can delay max 14 days, cannot amend |

### 29.6. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Legislative Council can be created/abolished by? | Council | Parliament by law under Art. 169 on resolution of State Assembly |
| 2017 | Prelims | Money Bill in state can be introduced only in? | Money Bill | Legislative Assembly |
| 2018 | Mains | Role of Legislative Council in states | Bicameralism | Revising chamber, representation of special interests |

### 29.7. MIND MAP

```text
STATE LEGISLATURE (ARTS. 168-212)
├── COMPOSITION: Governor + Assembly (+ Council if bicameral)
├── ASSEMBLY: Directly elected, 5 years, more powerful
├── COUNCIL: Permanent, 6 years, 1/3 retire, less powerful
└── FUNCTIONS: Legislation, financial control, executive accountability
```

