## 30. HIGH COURT

**[SYL: GS2-D.2] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 30] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 214-231]**

### 30.1. Introduction

High Court is the **highest court** of a state. Article 214 provides for every state. Articles 231 empowers Parliament to establish a common High Court for two or more states.

### 30.2. Composition (Art. 216)

Consists of a **Chief Justice** and other judges. President determines number of judges.

### 30.3. Appointment of Judges (Art. 217)

Appointed by **President** in consultation with Chief Justice of India and Governor of state. In case of appointment of Chief Justice, consultation with Governor also includes Chief Justice of the concerned High Court.

### 30.4. Tenure and Removal

- **Tenure:** Till age **62 years**.
- **Removal:** Same as Supreme Court judges - by impeachment for proved misbehaviour/incapacity (Art. 124(4) applied).
- **Transfer:** Can be transferred by President after consultation with CJI.

### 30.5. Jurisdiction and Powers

#### 30.5.1. Original Jurisdiction
Mostly in matters like writs (in some states), company law, matrimonial cases (as per statutes), etc.

#### 30.5.2. Appellate Jurisdiction
Hears appeals from subordinate courts in civil and criminal cases.

#### 30.5.3. Writ Jurisdiction (Art. 226)
**Very wide** - can issue writs for enforcement of Fundamental Rights as well as for other purposes (any legal right). This is broader than Art. 32.

#### 30.5.4. Superintendence over Subordinate Courts (Art. 227)
Power of superintendence over all courts and tribunals throughout the territories in relation to which it exercises jurisdiction.

#### 30.5.5. Other Powers
Court of record (Art. 215), power to punish for contempt, judicial review of state laws/executive actions.

### 30.6. Independence of High Court

Similar safeguards as Supreme Court - security of tenure, salaries charged on Consolidated Fund of State, removal only by impeachment, consultations in appointment.

### 30.7. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Writ jurisdiction of High Court is under which Article? | Writ | Article 226 |
| 2017 | Prelims | Age of retirement of High Court judge? | Tenure | 62 years |
| 2018 | Mains | Difference between Art. 32 and Art. 226 | Writ Jurisdiction | Art. 32 SC only for FRs, Art. 226 HC for FRs + other purposes |

### 30.8. MIND MAP

```text
HIGH COURT (ARTS. 214-231)
├── APPOINTMENT: By President (consultation with CJI, Governor, HC CJ)
├── TENURE: 62 years, removal by impeachment
├── JURISDICTION: Original, Appellate, Writ (Art. 226 - wider than SC), Superintendence (Art. 227)
└── COURT OF RECORD (Art. 215)
```

