## 31. SUBORDINATE COURTS

**[SYL: GS2-D.2] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 31] | [BARE ACT: Arts. 233-237]**

### 31.1. Introduction

Subordinate courts function below High Courts. Articles 233-237 deal with appointments, posting and promotion of persons working in district courts and below.

### 31.2. Structure of Subordinate Courts

- **District Courts:** Headed by District Judge. Deals with civil and criminal cases of district.
- **Civil Courts:** Sub-Judge, Munsif/Municipal Magistrate etc. as per Civil Courts Act.
- **Criminal Courts:** Chief Judicial Magistrate, Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, Judicial Magistrates of First/Second Class as per CrPC.
- **Special Courts:** Family Courts, Consumer Courts, Fast Track Courts, etc.

### 31.3. Appointment of District Judges (Art. 233)

Appointed by **Governor** of state in consultation with **High Court**. Can be from:
- Persons already in judicial service of state
- Advocates/pleaders with 7 years experience

### 31.4. Appointment of Other Judicial Officers (Art. 234)

Appointed by **Governor** in accordance with rules made by Governor in consultation with **State Public Service Commission** and **High Court**.

### 31.5. Control over Subordinate Courts (Art. 235)

**High Court** exercises control over district courts and courts subordinate thereto in all matters relating to posting, promotion and grant of leave to persons belonging to judicial service of state.

### 31.6. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Appointment of District Judges is done by? | Appointment | Governor in consultation with High Court (Art. 233) |
| 2017 | Prelims | Control over subordinate courts is exercised by? | Control | High Court (Art. 235) |

### 31.7. MIND MAP

```text
SUBORDINATE COURTS (ARTS. 233-237)
├── DISTRICT JUDGE: Appointed by Governor in consultation with HC (Art. 233)
├── OTHER JUDICIAL OFFICERS: By Governor in consultation with SPSC & HC (Art. 234)
├── CONTROL: HC exercises control over subordinate courts (Art. 235)
└── STRUCTURE: District Courts, Civil Courts, Criminal Courts, Special Courts
```

