## 35. FINANCE COMMISSION

**[SYL: GS2-E.3] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 35] | [BARE ACT: Art. 280]**

### 35.1. Introduction

Article 280 provides for Finance Commission - a **quasi-judicial** body constituted by President every 5 years (or earlier).

### 35.2. Composition

Chairman and 4 other members. Qualifications prescribed by Parliament.

### 35.3. Functions (Art. 280)

- Distribution of net proceeds of taxes between Centre and States (vertical devolution).
- Allocation between States of respective shares of such proceeds (horizontal devolution).
- Principles governing grants-in-aid to States from Consolidated Fund of India.
- Measures needed to augment Consolidated Fund of State to supplement resources of Panchayats and Municipalities.
- Any other matter referred by President in interest of sound finance.

### 35.4. Nature

- Constitutional body (Art. 280)
- Quasi-judicial in nature
- Recommendations are **advisory** (not binding on government)
- Acts as balancing wheel of fiscal federalism

### 35.5. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | Finance Commission is constituted under? | Art. 280 | Article 280 |
| 2017 | Mains | Role of Finance Commission in fiscal federalism | Devolution | Vertical/horizontal devolution, grants-in-aid |
| 2018 | Prelims | Finance Commission recommendations are? | Nature | Advisory, not binding |

### 35.6. MIND MAP

```text
FINANCE COMMISSION (ART. 280)
├── CONSTITUTIONAL, QUASI-JUDICIAL
├── CONSTITUTED EVERY 5 YEARS BY PRESIDENT
├── FUNCTIONS: Tax devolution, grants-in-aid, local bodies
└── RECOMMENDATIONS ADVISORY
```

