## 43. PANCHAYATI RAJ

**[SYL: GS2-F.1] | [LAXMIKANTH: Chapter 43] | [73RD AMENDMENT ACT, 1992]**

### 43.1. Historical Background

- Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957) - recommended 3-tier system (Gram Panchayat, Panchayat Samiti, Zila Parishad)
- Ashok Mehta Committee (1977) - recommended 2-tier system
- G.V.K. Rao Committee (1985) - made Panchayati Raj a 'third tier' of federal system
- L.M. Singhvi Committee (1986) - recommended constitutional status

### 43.2. 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992

Came into force on **24 April 1993**. Added **Part IX** and **Eleventh Schedule** (29 subjects).

#### 43.2.1. Salient Features
- **Three-tier system:** Village, Intermediate, District level (Art. 243B)
- **Election:** Direct elections to all seats (Art. 243C)
- **Reservation:** For SCs, STs in proportion to population; 1/3 seats for women (Art. 243D)
- **Duration:** 5 years, elections before expiry or within 6 months of dissolution (Art. 243E)
- **State Election Commission:** Conducts Panchayat elections (Art. 243K)
- **State Finance Commission:** Reviews financial position of Panchayats every 5 years (Art. 243I)
- **Powers and responsibilities:** As per State legislation for 29 subjects in Eleventh Schedule (Art. 243G)

### 43.3. Types of Panchayats
- **Gram Panchayat:** At village level
- **Panchayat Samiti:** At intermediate level (block)
- **Zila Parishad:** At district level

### 43.4. PYQs

| Year | Exam | Question | Topic | Approach |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2016 | Prelims | 73rd Amendment added which Part? | 73rd Amendment | Part IX |
| 2017 | Mains | Significance of 73rd Amendment in decentralization | Panchayati Raj | Constitutional status, reservation, regular elections |
| 2018 | Prelims | Eleventh Schedule contains? | Schedule | 29 subjects for Panchayats |

### 43.5. MIND MAP

```text
PANCHAYATI RAJ - 73RD AMENDMENT 1992
├── ADDED: Part IX, Eleventh Schedule (29 subjects)
├── THREE-TIER: Gram Panchayat, Panchayat Samiti, Zila Parishad
├── RESERVATION: SC/ST + 1/3 women
├── INSTITUTIONS: SEC, SFC
└── DIRECT ELECTIONS, 5 YEAR TERM
```

